rs","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mfschubert","id":30735893,"login":"mfschubert","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM1ODkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mfschubert","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"OK, I was actually able to work around this issue by `jit`-ing the call to `eig` and specifying CPU. There don't seem to be any downsides here, so I will close this issue.\r\n\r\n```\r\ndef _eig_host(matrix: jnp.ndarray) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\r\n    \"\"\"Wraps numpy.linalg.eig so that it can be jit-ed on a machine with GPUs.\"\"\"\r\n    eigenvalues_shape = jax.ShapeDtypeStruct(matrix.shape[:-1], complex)\r\n    eigenvectors_shape = jax.ShapeDtypeStruct(matrix.shape, complex)\r\n    return host_callback.call(\r\n        # We force this computation to be performed on the cpu by jit-ing and\r\n        # explicitly specifying the device.\r\n        jax.jit(jnp.linalg.eig, device=jax.devices(\"cpu\")[0]),\r\n        matrix,\r\n        result_shape=[eigenvalues_shape, eigenvectors_shape],\r\n    )\r\n```","created_at":"2022-10-31T16:18:53Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/13046#issuecomment-1297339388","id":1297339388,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/13046","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5NU9P8","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray